desktop-shell-application-style-export(1)

# NAME

desktop-shell-application-style-export - gives other programs the shared look

# SYNOPSIS

*desktop-shell-application-style-export* [*-c* _FILE_] [*--print-launcher-arguments*]

# DESCRIPTION

*desktop-shell-application-style-export* reads the established look - the
shipped defaults, then the colors and font of the sway bar found through
_$SWAYSOCK_, then the variables in
_$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components/shared-theme.css_ - writes it into
other programs' per-user style files and exits:

- _gtk-3.0/gtk.css_: a complete, flat style for GTK 3 applications;
- _gtk-4.0/gtk.css_: named colors and libadwaita color variables only, since
  a user style sheet outranks every program's own;
- the _gtk-application-prefer-dark-theme_ and _gtk-font-name_ keys of
  _gtk-3.0/settings.ini_ and _gtk-4.0/settings.ini_, keeping the others;
- _swaylock/config_ and _swaynag/config_;
- copies of the icons named by *recolored-icons*, Adwaita's single-color
  icons recolored to the text color, in
  _$XDG_DATA_HOME/icons/Adwaita/symbolic/CONTEXT/NAME-symbolic.svg_, which the
  toolkit reads before the system's copy. Programs such as Thunar's side
  pane show these icons as they are, so the dark gray would disappear on a
  dark background. Full-color icons and the selected theme do not change.
  Only the foreground gray is replaced; icons with scripts, links or
  entities, or larger than 64 KiB, are skipped. Copies no longer listed are
  removed, never files without the marker;
- the GSettings keys _color-scheme_ and _font-name_ of
  _org.gnome.desktop.interface_, when that schema is installed.

All paths are inside _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME_, the icons inside _$XDG_DATA_HOME_.
A file is written only when it does not exist or its first line is this
program's marker; delete the marker line to keep a file as your own. Files are replaced atomically, with mode
0644, never through a symbolic link or a linked folder leading outside
_$XDG_CONFIG_HOME_, and only when their contents change. No privilege is
needed or used.

# OPTIONS

*-h, --help*
	Show the help message and exit.

*-c, --config* _FILE_
	Read settings from _FILE_ instead of the usual places.

*-s, --style* _FILE_
	Accepted like by every component; unused.

*--print-launcher-arguments*
	Print the font and color options of the *wmenu* launcher, shell-quoted,
	instead of writing files.

# CONFIGURATION

The installed _@sysconfdir@/sway/config.d/60-desktop-shell-application-style-export.conf_
runs the program on every sway start and reload.

# SETTINGS

Read from _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components/application-style-export.ini_,
else _/etc/xdg/desktop-shell-components/application-style-export.ini_. All
are optional.

*[export]*
	*enabled* = _true_|_false_++
	*gtk3*, *gtk4*, *gtk-settings*, *gsettings*, *lock-screen*, *prompts*, *recolor-icons* = _true_|_false_++
	*color-scheme* = _auto_|_dark_|_light_

*[icons]*
	*recolored-icons* = icon names separated by *;*, without *-symbolic*

# SEE ALSO

*sway*(5), *swaylock*(1), *swaynag*(5), *wmenu*(1)
